# Hall of Echoes copying a creature that is itself a copy: "If the copied creature is copying something else, then Hall
# of Echoes becomes a copy of whatever that creature copied" (the ruling, CR 707.3), exceptions included (CR 707.9b), and
# "it doesn't copy whether that creature is tapped or untapped" (the ruling). On turn 3 Bot1's Likeness Looter loots
# (tapping) and becomes a copy of Embereth Shieldbreaker "except it has flying and this ability"; then Bot1 pays {5} for
# the Hall at it. The Hall becomes an Embereth Shieldbreaker with flying too - a 2/1 red Human Knight - and stays
# untapped beside the tapped Looter.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Likeness Looter
Embereth Shieldbreaker
Sol Ring
Black Lotus
Hall of Echoes
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain x20

